{
  "format": "berreman-stack",
  "version": 1,
  "title": "Monoclinic beta-Ga2O3, (010) surface, infrared reflection",
  "source": "M. Schubert et al., Phys. Rev. B 93, 125209 (2016), Tables II and IV; sample (010) at azimuth P1 of Fig. 5",
  "notes": "The dielectric tensor is Eqs. 21a-e: eps_inf plus 8 Bu oscillators polarised in the a-c plane at angle alpha from a (x), 4 Au oscillators along b, and a Drude term per Cartesian axis. Coordinates as the paper's Fig. 2: x along a, y along c* (in the a-c plane, normal to a), z along -b. Parameters from Table II (Bu and Au TO modes) and Table IV (eps_inf, plasma broadening), with the isotropic plasma frequency 1058.3 cm-1 of Sec. IV B. The tables print the last significant digit in parentheses: 266.(2) is 266.2, 81(0) is 810, 37(0) is 370. CORRECTION: Table IV's columns for a and c* are switched. P. Gopalan et al., arXiv:2010.03107 (2020), with Schubert as a co-author, says on p. 4 that 'due to a misprint, values reported in Ref. 16 for permittivity parameters corresponding to a and c* were accidentally switched'; so eps_inf here is 3.21 along a and 3.75 along c*. The amplitudes A of Table II enter Eq. 10 squared (to the first power the oscillators would add almost nothing). With both, this file reproduces the paper's own derived numbers, which the managed tests check: the static constants (Table IV with a and c* switched back), all 12 LO frequencies of Table II, and the 5 Au LPP frequencies of Table III. The Bu LO angles of Table II agree when read as measured from c*, not a. The Bu LPP frequencies of Table III are not reproduced (the highest is 924.6 cm-1 here, as the paper's Fig. 12 shows, against 967.1 in the table); the tests only print them. Orientation: the paper's lab frame (z into the sample, plane of incidence x-z) and Euler matrices (Eqs. 31-33) are this program's, so P1 is euler [62.5, 0.4, 0] as the caption of Fig. 5 gives. Fig. 5 (P1, P2, P3 at 50, 60 and 70 degrees) is compared at 17 features of M41, M42 and M43 read off the figure, in the reststrahlen band. All agree in sign and, within reading accuracy, in size; M41 and M43 fixed the sign of S3 in the program's Mueller convention, and M42 is the independent check. This confirms the paper's Euler angles and p and s are the program's. NOT REPRODUCED: above about 900 cm-1 the computed off-diagonal elements reach 0.5 (at 1000 cm-1, where the computed reflectance falls to 0.05), while the figure shows nearly 0 there; the cause is not known.",
  "units": { "length": "um", "spectral": "cm-1" },
